   "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vincentsch/explainroo/zipball/v0.1.0",
   "body": "First release.\n\nexplainroo lets your coding agent make narrated explainer videos and product demos. You tell the agent what the video should explain. It writes the narration and a bit of JavaScript that draws each scene, and explainroo turns them into an MP4 on your own computer.\n\nWhat is in it:\n\n- A local voice (Kokoro, 28 voices) and word timing (Whisper), so pictures appear when the voice names them. No account and no API key.\n- Five looks: paper, clean, chalk, blueprint and midnight.\n- Sizes for YouTube, Shorts, TikTok, Reels, Instagram and LinkedIn, with captions for vertical and square videos.\n- `pace` to make a whole video quicker or slower.\n- Product demos: `s.ui` draws an app's screens again in its own colors and fonts, with a cursor that clicks and types.\n- Checks an agent can use without watching: stills, contact sheets, a layout check and a speech check of the final mix.\n\nThe videos attached here were made with explainroo. Their sources are in `examples/`:\n\n- `explainroo-intro.mp4`: explainroo in 86 seconds (paper look)\n- `unspar-demo.mp4`: a product demo for Unspar\n- `how-dns-works.mp4`: how DNS finds a website (chalk look)\n- `merge-vs-rebase.mp4`: git merge vs rebase (midnight look, vertical with captions)\n\nMore examples, including unofficial demos of Gmail, ChatGPT and Claude, are on https://www.explainroo.com/videos/\n\nGet started: point your agent at this repo, or clone it, run `npm install` and `node bin/explainroo.js doctor --fetch`, then ask your agent for a video. It is developed and tested on Linux; macOS and Windows should work but have had less testing.\n"
